<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Maitland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1760">1760</a>–<a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Thomas Maitland, Thomas Maitland (British Army officer), King Tom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Thomas Maitland was a British general and colonial governor who served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> from 1805 to 1811 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> from 1813. From 1815 he was also the first Lord High Commissioner of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of the Ionian Islands, where his autocratic manner earned him the nickname King Tom. He imposed the constitution of 1817, which left the islands' assembly and senate little real power. He died in Malta in 1824.</p></div>
